WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.560
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.730
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.990
Babies, clean out those ears and listen up!

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.490
This is big news!

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.660
Okay!

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:22.000
The annual Soccer World Tournament is going to be held once again at Kibougaoka Stadium.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:28.130
And as is tradition, Four Star Academy's first-years will star in its halftime show.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.630
Get ready to get on it!

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.130
Halftime show?

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:38.140
Yes, there's a break between the first and second halves of the game.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:44.020
To entertain the fans in the stadium during that break, they hold a halftime show.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.520
We'll be holding an audition for it right away.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.030
Submit your entry sheets via your Aikatsu Mobiles.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.530
Yes!

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.570
A halftime show...

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.060
What? You're relocating to Italy?

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.850
Yeah, this assignment seems like it might go on for a while.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:56.860
We were talking, and we thought that it would be nice if we could all go as a family.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.370
Italy, huh...

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.120
I've always wanted to go, but...

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.500
Yume-chan! Yume-chan!

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.040
Hey, wake up!

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.420
The results of the first audition are out!

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.300
Yume-chan!

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.010
Really?

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.300
Yeah!

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.560
Look.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.720
We both made it!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.480
Yeah, this is great.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.810
Yay!

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:39.320
Anna-sensei said that the S4 members and all the admins were chosen to be in this show before.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.450
Right, it's like the gateway to success.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:46.950
I know! Wait, what kind of gate is the gateway to success?

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:59.090
Could this be the gateway to success you were talking about?

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:05.010
That phrase is actually a metaphor for the hardships you need to face

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:09.770
before finally reaching success at the end of a thorny path.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:13.480
I get it. Now I'm actually excited.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.980
Rola!

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.990
Yume, Koharu! Over here!

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:24.910
You're here early.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.070
More like you're late.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.580
Anyway, I'm so glad that we all managed to pass.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:30.540
Yeah!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.750
Well, in my case there was never any doubt I would make it.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.460
And of course, the center position will be mine.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.460
Center?

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.920
Was it not on the audition results sheet?

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.090
There will be one center for each class.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.050
Didn't you read it?

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:51.470
I got too hyped after seeing that I passed.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.980
Don't be surprised when I become the center for Theater Class.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.730
The center...

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.280
Yes, I will be Song Class's center!{let's just do it like this, it'll make things less cupsmarty in the long run}

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:06.780
If I were a mountain, it would be Mount Fuji!

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:14.910
Nijino Yume, were you listening to me?

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.540
Huh? Which part?

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:25.170
I know, it means that Rola and I will be facing off to be the Song Class center.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.550
That gets me going. I won't be losing this time.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:30.930
That's exactly what I wanted to hear!

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:34.480
And Mahiru-chan and I will be competing too.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.020
I want to go out with a bang one last time.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.690
Huh? Last time?

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.690
Oh, forget I said anything.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.320
First, congratulations on passing the audition.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:53.410
The halftime show is a highly anticipated event,

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.460
and as the bar is raised every year, expectations are high.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:00.210
Work hard to put on a show they'll never forget.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.540
Yes!

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:06.880
We'll split you up into your classes and begin lessons right away.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:11.470
In one week, we'll decide who gets to be the center for each class.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.600
Today was really exhausting.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:26.280
Yeah. The halftime show is twenty whole minutes long, but it feels like they're not wasting a single second.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:27.900
It's kind of surprising.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:33.740
And hearing how polished they want this show to be makes me feel really invested.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.080
Me too.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:42.540
Actually, Yume-chan, I'm invested in this for a slightly different reason.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:52.510
Well, you see, I'm probably going to be moving to Italy after this show because of my father's work.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:56.600
I'd personally like to stay behind here at school,

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:02.310
but because we don't know when he'll be back, my mom and I decided to go along with him.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:07.030
Besides, I'm sure I can study fashion while I'm in Italy anyway.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:12.820
Yume-chan?

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:17.830
Are you asleep?

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.220
Look!

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.600
This is the show from when Hime-senpai's year did it.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.350
I figured Hime-senpai would be Song Class's center.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.850
Her presence is overwhelming.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:44.110
Tsubasa-senpai's acting is wonderful as well.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:48.610
Yozora-senpai is so handsome!{this is both fine and not fine}{I swear I only thought this but didn't write it...}

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:52.530
And this is from when Yuzu-senpai participated.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:57.870
I really respect how she can dance so fiercely with a smile on her face.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:02.870
I'm gonna be the center and get one step closer to S4!

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:07.710
Not so fast, Yume. You'll have to beat me before you can say that.

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:10.380
I know, and I don't plan on losing.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.640
We've got more lessons tomorrow.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:17.050
Yeah. So...

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:21.100
Hime-senpai was so awesome in that video.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.100
I hope I can be even a fraction as good as her.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.400
Me too.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.150
I'm going to be the center no matter what!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.280
I know you can do it.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.240
Why's that?

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:38.280
Well, you always seem to get a special surge whenever the pressure's on.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.290
Yeah, I guess you're right. Thanks, Koharu-chan.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.790
Weren't you about to say something just now?

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:48.880
Do you want some candy?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:52.920
Sure! I can never say no to something sweet.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:54.590
Actually, Yume-chan,

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.760
didn't you just have pancakes at the cafeteria?

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.850
Sweets are the source of a girl's energy!

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:09.980
A dress to match the stadium stage...

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.700
Perfect! This is the one.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.730
Today was overwhelming again.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:49.650
I think what you need is some sweets energy, Yume-chan.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.860
That's right! And hey, speak for yourself.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.650
You got it.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:59.740
One moment, please. I'll run a full search of my brain database.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.740
Tick tick tick tick...

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.240
Ding-dong!

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:07.290
I believe there's a nearby cafe with delectable cream puffs!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:10.000
Yay! Thanks, Ako-chan!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.880
I haven't been able to get over how delicious Subaru-kyun looked the other day...

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.090
Oh, I'm just speaking to myself.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:19.760
Let's stop by there then, okay?

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.350
Sorry, I'm going to head back for the night.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:23.810
Me too.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.310
Huh, you are? That's too bad.

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:28.890
See you tomorrow.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:32.570
Bye, Yume. Make sure not to eat too much.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.030
And here I was planning to eat your share too, Rola.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.780
Tomorrow is our center audition.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:40.820
I know.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.620
Are you sure you don't want to go?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:45.580
Huh?

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:48.160
It's just that you're always together.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.080
You and Yume.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:53.540
Yeah, but that might have been a mistake.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:54.170
What?

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:58.670
This time, I definitely don't want to lose to Yume.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.970
I don't think I can win by training the same way as her.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:09.060
So this time, I'm trying to Aikatsu many times harder than Yume to improve myself.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.770
That's why I can't be with her.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:17.820
Somehow, I think I understand what you're going through.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.820
Do you want to join me for a lesson?

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:22.780
Thanks.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.830
Right now?

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:29.370
Yes. Tomorrow is the center audition.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:31.960
We'd like to train a bit more on our own.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.580
All right.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:37.210
Remember that working too hard can backfire.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.050
Keep it within reason.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.510
We will, thank you.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.930
But it won't happen again. {I can change the line in ep 22 so that this one says "But I won't lose again". what do you think?}{either is fijn}

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:57.650
You don't want to lose to Nijino Yume, huh.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.330
<i>I'll do everything that I need to.</i>

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:09.080
<i>I don't want to have any more regrets!</i>

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:28.100
We're going to have you actually take the stage during halftime of today's game.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:33.100
We'll use that to decide who gets to be the center

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:36.110
at the Soccer World Tournament finals.{for "finals" instead of "championship match" but it would be "final" in non-america and most people who care about soccer are non-america}

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:37.110
Yes!

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:41.360
Your performance will be evaluated by a panel of judges

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.990
and the crowd present in the stands.{why are there twelve players on each side}

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.960
Song Class is up first.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:56.500
Yeah. I'm starting to get nervous.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:58.790
Do your best, Yume-chan.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:12:59.800
I will!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:02.010
Wait, where's Rola?

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.520
Song Class is about to go on.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:19.400
I'm going to confirm you're all here, so please step forward.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:20.270
Okay.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.030
Oh, yes!

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:26.030
That'll do it for the first half!

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:30.030
Now for the halftime show you've all been waiting for.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:35.040
Which idols will be chosen to take the center position during the finals?

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.670
It looks like you're missing one member.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:40.630
Does anybody know where she is?

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.840
<i>Rola, where are you?{what befell}</i>

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:44.630
Sorry I'm late!

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:46.430
Rola!

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:48.930
You barely made it. Get it together.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:49.930
I will.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:53.390
Where did you go? I was worried.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.180
Nowhere in particular.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:59.520
<i>Yume, I'm not going to lose. I don't want to lose!</i>

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:03.320
Rola, you seem off.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:04.440
Now then,

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:09.450
compete with everything you have and leave nothing on the table!{I think you're mixing metaphors}{I always google to make sure, dammit!}

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:10.570
Yes!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.880
A princess coord emitting pastel elegance, {couldn't exactly find this "ojousama coord" by name}

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:23.590
accented by a book print on the skirt.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:29.800
A cool, dark rock coord inspired by the streets of London

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:32.720
with a ribbon on the breast to provide a cute contrast.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.600
Yume, I'm not gonna lose!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.980
It's my time to shine!

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.650
<i>Rola is serious.</i>

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.060
<i>I don't want to lose either!</i>

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:44.730
Nijino Yume, ready to go!

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:22.710
Rola picked a dress that matched the stadium stage.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:25.460
Yume-chan's dress is cute too.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:29.090
Well, I must admit they probably look the next best after me.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:10.520
Has everyone made their decisions?

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:13.150
Please put in your votes now!

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:17.650
Now, who will top Song Class?

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:20.910
It looks like Nijino Yume-san is on her way there.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.790
But how will it play out in the end?

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:36.170
There it is! Nijino Yume-san will be Song Class's center!{can center be a verb}

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.340
I did it!

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:40.430
Great job, Yume-chan!

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.510
Congrats, Yume.

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:43.680
You're pretty good.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:45.220
Thanks!

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:46.680
You were really cute up there.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.940
Even I have to applaud your performance.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:56.650
All right, Theater Class is up next.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:19:01.070
Nijino Yume, the next person to claim a center position

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.080
will be none other than me!

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.700
Huh?

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.830
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:09.120
Where did Rola go?

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:13.250
Don't you think it'd be hard for her to face you after losing?

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.840
That can't be true!

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:19.720
Rola and I might be fierce rivals, 
but before that we're close friends!

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.470
Isn't that exactly why?

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:33.440
<i>Why... I tried so hard.</i>

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:39.240
<i>I separated myself from Yume and did so much more Aikatsu than her...</i>

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.860
<i>Why couldn't I win?</i>

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:45.950
Sakuraba.

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.200
Anna-sensei.

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:51.500
Too bad about the result.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:53.630
I...

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:58.630
I... didn't want to lose to Yume again.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:03.260
That's why I trained so much harder than her.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:05.050
But in the end...

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:08.520
Did you think that's all it'd take to win?

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:14.270
Sakuraba, don't I keep telling you that you're different from Nijino?

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.020
Your individuality is most important.

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:23.280
Then are you saying that I'll never be able to beat Yume's individuality no matter how hard I try?!

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.910
Nothing of the sort.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.290
Each individual is unique.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.500
No two things in the world are perfectly alike.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.500
Nijino has her individuality,

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:42.050
and you have your own individuality as well, Sakuraba.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.590
Anna-sensei...

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:50.810
You don't need to measure yourself against Nijino, do the same things as her, or worry about winning and losing.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:55.310
More importantly, it's nonsense to think you'll never beat her.

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:59.610
You simply need to shine in a way that only you can.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:04.990
Compete by doing things in each of your own ways.{this is liable to be repeated in enough contexts that metaphoring could anaesthetic}{I'm fine with 'way'}

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:08.580
That's what it means to be true rivals.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.950
The others are waiting for you.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:19.670
Shine by doing things my own way...

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:27.220
The votes are in, and the winner is...

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:34.100
There! Saotome Ako-san will be Theater Class's center!

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:36.600
Thank you, everyone!

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.860
Ako-chan was great!

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:41.860
Rola! Where have you been?

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:45.110
Ako-chan is Theater Class's center.

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:46.780
Yume, congratulations.

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.870
Yeah, thanks!

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:55.000
Yume, starting today, we're going to be true rivals.

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:03.630
Everyone from Beauty Class, you're next.

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.260
Please get ready.

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:06.880
We've got to go.

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:08.840
Yeah.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:13.890
Hang on. Weren't we always rivals?

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:16.180
It's a little different from before. {apparently from is more correct}

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:18.480
What do you mean?

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:21.900
It means I'll be doing things my own way.

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:13.010
I don't want Koharu-chan to leave.

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.180
Sorry, but the decision's been made.

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:17.930
What can I do for her before it's too late?

00:24:17.930 --> 00:24:20.270
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.270 --> 00:24:21.940
Rainbow Candy.

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:24.310
Become the first-star idol!
